# Every text file is checked out with LF line endings, whatever core.autocrlf says.
#
# Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true system-wide, which checks text out
# with CRLF. Several checks compare committed files byte for byte: the OpenAPI
# artifact against its generation, golden IR digests, and sqlx's checksums of
# migration files. So a CRLF checkout failed them on Windows while Linux passed.
# The index already holds LF; this only fixes what a checkout writes.
* text=auto eol=lf
